==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] A1 nabla_mu T_c^mu_t = -(rho_t + 3(rho+p)A_t/A) and nabla_mu T_c^mu_i = (rho+p) d_i ln N + d_i p on the general u-adapted chart
         measured: sympy identity: True
         reading:  so 'nabla T_c = Q u' gives: rho_t + 3 (rho+p) A_t/A = N Q  (energy) and (rho+p) d_i ln N + d_i p = 0 (Euler; Q u_i = 0 in this chart)
  [PASS] A2 vacuum T^{mu nu} = -rho_L g^{mu nu}: nabla_mu T_vac^mu_nu = -d_nu rho_L (all four components)
         measured: sympy identity: True
         reading:  with nabla T_vac = -Q u: d_nu rho_L = Q u_nu: in this chart d_i rho_L = 0 and d_t rho_L = -N Q.  The vacuum is uniform on the hypersurfaces orthogonal to u_c.
  Euler equation on the chart with N = -rho_L,t / Q(rho_L, rho_c)  [x-component]:
       (-(p(t, x, y, z) + rho(t, x, y, z))*Derivative(Q(rLt(t), rho(t, x, y, z)), rho(t, x, y, z))*Derivative(rho(t, x, y, z), x) + Q(rLt(t), rho(t, x, y, z))*Derivative(p(t, x, y, z), x))/Q(rLt(t), rho(t, x, y, z))
  dust (p = 0): -rho(t, x, y, z)*Derivative(Q(rLt(t), rho(t, x, y, z)), rho(t, x, y, z))*Derivative(rho(t, x, y, z), x)/Q(rLt(t), rho(t, x, y, z))
  d_x ln N = -Derivative(Q(rLt(t), rho(t, x, y, z)), rho(t, x, y, z))*Derivative(rho(t, x, y, z), x)/Q(rLt(t), rho(t, x, y, z))
  [PASS] A3-dust for DUST the Euler equation reads  rho_c Q_rho d_x rho_c / Q = 0: either Q_rho = 0 (Q a function of Lambda only) or rho_c has no spatial gradient on the fluid-orthogonal slice
         measured: d_x ln N = -(Q_rho d_x rho_c)/Q  (sympy); no term from Lambda (d_x rho_L = 0)
         reading:  STRUCTURE THEOREM: with a Lorentz-invariant vacuum and a Q u^mu exchange, dust with Q_rho != 0 cannot carry density contrasts
  barotropic fluid: dp/drho_c = (rho + p) Q_rho / Q  =>  c_s^2 = Q_rho*(p + rho)/Q
  power law Q = xi rho_c^n rho_L^m : c_s^2 = n*(p + rho)/rho
  ODE  d(rho+p)/drho = 1 + n (rho+p)/rho  -> Eq(h(rho), (C1*rho**n*(n - 1) - rho)/(n - 1))
  [PASS] A4 the EOS forced by Q = xi rho_c^n rho_L^m is p = n rho/(1-n) + C rho^n  (w = n/(1-n): a constant-w fluid plus C rho^n)
         measured: sympy dsolve: True
         reading:  so 'cold' (w -> 0, c_s^2 -> 0) requires n -> 0, i.e. Q independent of rho_c; the stiffness of the exchange IS the pressure
  static fluid (rho_t = 0, A_t = 0, mean flow at rest): the energy equation Dc_t = Q u_t = -N Q gives  N Q = 0  -> Q = [0]
  [PASS] A5 in a stationary halo with the mean flow at rest, the fluid energy equation forces Q = 0; with a definite sign (vacuum -> matter, Q >= 0) a stationary halo with no net radial flux has Q = 0 everywhere (integral of Q over the halo = the mass flux out)
         measured: sympy: Q = [0]
         reading:  so the exchange cannot SUSTAIN a profile: it can act only in time-dependent phases (formation history), which this door does not compute (untested); in equilibrium Q = 0, d_mu rho_L = 0 and N is unconstrained (the theorem A3 applies only where Q != 0)

